{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#3412","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#3412","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#3412\",\"parent_revision\":\"4cbb9f6b43b884b1ce32bad10c5500bf7310794a68460cbfe2dc52e67caa216f\",\"root_revision\":\"4cbb9f6b43b884b1ce32bad10c5500bf7310794a68460cbfe2dc52e67caa216f\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P2\\ntype: Refactor\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-09-04\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\n`FileCache._work_item_snapshots()` logs a `_log.warning` for each corrupt/unparseable snapshot it skips, but surfaces no machine-readable count to its one caller (`GitHubWorkItemsBackend.load_records`, `backends/github_work_items.py:564`). Its own docstring says this mirrors `_CacheStateStore._salvage_field`'s per-entry salvage policy for the durable mutation queue \u2014 but that queue-side policy also feeds a rejection count into `ReconcileOutcome.rejected_mutations`, which is threaded through `sync_state.py`, `tool_responses.py`, and surfaced in `backlog_sync`'s response. The snapshot-side policy has no equivalent.\\n\\nImpact: a user running a sync/reconcile with one or more corrupt local snapshots sees the affected item(s) silently disappear from `load_records()`'s output, with only a WARNING log line as a trace \u2014 easy to miss entirely when running as an MCP server subprocess (no captured stdout/stderr surfaced to the calling agent).\\n\\nNot fixed as part of PR #3405 (the 0-byte-tmp-file crash fix) because doing so properly would mean widening `_work_item_snapshots`'s return shape (or adding an out-parameter/counter), updating its one caller, and then threading that count through the sync/reconcile response chain the same way `rejected_mutations` already is \u2014 a materially larger change than the crash fix itself.\\n\\nUser-provided context: the `rejected_mutations` plumbing (`models.py`, `sync_engine.py`, `sync_state.py`, `tool_responses.py`) is the precedent to follow for shape and naming (e.g. a parallel `skipped_snapshots` count). Exact design is grooming/architecture work.\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Code review on PR #3405 (cache-crash fix)\\n- **Priority**: P2\\n- **Added**: 2026-09-04\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"6beedf0259ac7f8c9264b2c95e0cec9ed5c6c6cc4ae95c17ced3f655f52f0db5\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABStooaA\"}"}